1.What is an Array?
An array is a collection of elements of the same data type stored in contiguous memory locations.
It allows random access using an index.

1.1 Characteristics:
Fixed size (once declared, size cannot change)
Stores elements of same data type
Index starts from 0
Access time is O(1)

Example Interview Answer:
“An array is a data structure that stores multiple values of the same type in a single variable,
and we can access each element by its index starting from 0.”

2. How to Declare and Initialize Array
Declaration:
int[] arr;   // preferred
int arr2[];  // also valid

2.1Initialization (at declaration):
int[] arr = {1,2,3,4,5};
Initialization (later):
int[] arr = new int[5]; // size 5, default values 0
arr[0] = 10;
arr[1] = 20;